---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import Address from '../components/Address.astro'
import { PAGES } from '../data/pages'
import { COMPANY } from '../data/company'
---

<Legal
  page={PAGES.privacy}
  h1="Privacy policy"
  intro="Ferrocast is built to keep your data on your own computer. This page explains the few things that do leave it, where they go and why."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your overlays, alerts, commands, viewer notes and history stay on your computer.</li>
    <li>
      Sign-in tokens for Twitch, YouTube and Kick are kept in your operating system’s keychain.
    </li>
    <li>
      Our relay does three jobs: it receives Kick events, handles Kick sign-in, and hosts tip pages.
    </li>
    <li>
      Kick events (including chat) and tip notices wait on the relay only while your app is offline,
      for up to 7 days, and are then deleted. Nothing else from your stream is kept.
    </li>
    <li>Payment details stay with the payment provider. We never see card or UPI details.</li>
    <li>This website has no analytics, no tracking cookies and no third-party scripts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {COMPANY.legalName} is responsible for the data described here. Contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The desktop app</h2>
  <p>
    The app runs on your computer. Everything it stores (settings, overlays, alert rules, media,
    commands, the event log, viewer notes and tip history) is saved in a database on your own disk.
    We cannot see it. You can export it or delete it at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you connect Twitch, YouTube or Kick, you sign in on the platform’s own website. The access
    tokens the platform gives back are stored in your operating system’s keychain, never in plain
    files, exports or logs. The app talks to Twitch and YouTube directly from your computer.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app checks for updates by downloading a public release list. That request includes your IP
    address and the app version, as any download does. We do not attach an identifier to it.
  </p>

  <h2>YouTube</h2>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <p>
    Ferrocast uses YouTube API Services. When you connect YouTube, the app reads your live chat and stream events and carries out the moderation actions you choose, all from your computer. By connecting YouTube you also agree to the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>. You can disconnect in Settings → Accounts, or revoke Ferrocast’s access at any time on your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google account permissions page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Ferrocast relay</h2>
  <p>
    Some things can only reach a public address on the internet, so we run a small relay. It does
    three jobs:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Kick events.</strong> Kick sends follows, subs, chat messages and similar events only
      to a public address. The relay checks each one is really from Kick and forwards it to your app
      straight away. If your app is offline, events wait in a queue for up to 7 days and are then
      deleted. Once delivered, they are gone from the relay.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Kick sign-in.</strong> Kick’s sign-in needs a secret key that cannot ship inside an
      app, so the relay holds it. When you sign in to Kick, and when your sign-in is refreshed, your
      Kick tokens pass through the relay on their way to your app. They are not stored there.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tip pages.</strong> The relay serves your tip page and receives payment notices from
      Razorpay, Stripe or Ko-fi. See the next section for exactly what that involves.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The relay also keeps short technical logs (time, request type, an account id, IP address and
    errors) for up to 14 days to keep the service working and safe. These logs never contain chat
    text, tip messages or a tipper’s contact details.
  </p>

  <h2>Tip pages</h2>
  <p>
    Your tip page shows the display name you choose. Your legal name is never shown on your tip page
    or in your alerts. The payment provider’s checkout and receipt show the name on your provider
    account, so use a business or brand name there if you want to keep your own name private.
  </p>
  <p>When a viewer tips, the tip page server receives:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>their IP address, as any website does;</li>
    <li>the name they choose to show, their message and the amount;</li>
    <li>
      the payment status from the provider, which may include the payer’s email address or phone
      number. We use these only to match the payment to the tip.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Card, UPI and bank details are entered on the provider’s own checkout and never reach us. The
    tip notice is forwarded to your app and deleted from the relay once delivered, or after 7 days
    if your app stays offline. The payer’s email address and phone number are never forwarded to you
    and are deleted with the notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Ferrocast Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Pro is not on sale yet. When it is, we will need an email address for your account and will
    receive billing records from Razorpay (what you bought, when, and the payment status, not your
    card or UPI details). Pro features that sync your setup will store a copy of it on our servers,
    encrypted in transit and at rest, and only while you use them. This policy will be updated with
    the details before Pro launches.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    ferrocast.clearcraftlabs.com is a static site. It sets no cookies and loads nothing from other
    companies: fonts and images are served from the same address. It stores one setting in your
    browser, your light or dark theme choice, which never leaves your device. Our hosting provider
    may keep standard server logs (IP address, page, time) for security, for a short period.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or rent personal data, and we do not use it for advertising. We share data only
    with the services needed to run what you ask for (hosting for the relay, Razorpay for Pro
    payments) or when the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what data we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, and withdraw consent
    at any time. Users in India have these rights under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act,
    2023; users in the EU and UK have them under the GDPR. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a> and we will answer within
    {COMPANY.responseDays} working days and act within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>
    Ferrocast’s hosted services (the relay, tip pages and Pro) are for people aged 18 or over. If
    you are under 18, you may use them only with the consent of a parent or lawful guardian, who
    agrees to this policy for you. We do not knowingly process a child’s data without that consent.
    Streaming platforms also set their own age limits.
  </p>

  <h2>Grievance officer</h2>
  <p>
    For complaints under Indian law, contact our grievance officer: {COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.name},
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.email}`}>{COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that matters, we will update the date at the top and note the
    change in the app’s release notes.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <Address />
</Legal>
